hi everyone mad luigi here with another  elden ring video today discussing not an  aspect of the game but of the community  elden ring is a beautiful game with  wonderful art and visual design so it  shouldn't come as a surprise that the  game has inspired a whole host of  wonderful fan art i've been fortunate  enough to feature a lot of that art in  my video thumbnails and today i want to  take a moment to celebrate this artistic  aspect of the community from my first  lore video i've gotten the chance to  showcase some stunning fan art my godric  video featured a slightly abstract  character study of the grafted lord this  piece was made by alex langenick before  the game came out they have an instagram  and a personal website showcasing more  art in a similar style which i think  does a great job of capturing moods and  feelings in its own very stylized way  unfortunately there don't look to be any  more else in ring pieces but a lot of  the other work does fit right in with  the similar dark oppressive and weird  themes of the game  next is from my morgue video which  features a stunning depiction of the  grace given king with all his melancholy  and sense of duty oozing from the art  this piece was done by a user coasting  on twitter who also has a tumblr page  for their art they have other art in the  same style not only from eldon ring but  also from other fromsoft games like  securo and dark souls the morgot piece  might still be my favorite with its  great capturing of emotion but the cute  kali and pod pieces are pretty great too  after morgot comes the great second  elden lord ratagan drawn by one of the  most prolific fan artists in the  community shimek you can find more of  their art on their twitter or instagram  pages in addition to being able to  purchase prints on sites like redbubble  they have a whole host of wonderful  pieces on many of the significant  characters of eldon ring tons of bosses  the player character and even let me  solo her have found artful depictions  here and i can't recommend checking out  this work enough it's really great and  some custom pieces have even been  featured by other elden ring content  creators like smotown and oro boris  back to the cuter side of things my  torrent video features a picture of art  from march 3 range who posts their art  on instagram the work i used is a warm  snapshot of melania riding touring and  while there aren't other elden ring  works there are plenty of similarly cute  and warming works of art on their page  with topics ranging from characters to  people to snacks food and even a prawn  which one could say counts as elden ring  art finally the last piece of art i've  gotten to feature on my channel so far  is a wonderful depiction of the festival  of radon by the talented adrian le cause  you can find adrian's works on instagram  and you can purchase print files on  patreon or redbubble the style is  reminiscent of works depicting epics  with many character studies of the  important players in the lands between  the amount of detail and storytelling  that adrian is able to aesthetically fit  into the works depicting ronnie mikala  and melania is stunning a wonderful  blend of unique art and impressive  detail  so those are all of the artists that you  have seen on my channel and there are  plenty more either doing one-offs of  eldon ring content or consistently  putting out game related works as a  member of the community eldon ring is a  beautiful game with a ton of  eye-catching vistas and landscapes  seeing inspires so many additional  artists is fantastic and i think it  really adds to the experience of the  game to get to see and appreciate this  fan art if you're looking to see more  simply googling elden ring fan art  brings up a lot of results and you can  whittle it down by specifying a certain  character or game area you can also  check out the elden ring subreddit as  that's where i've seen a lot of these  great pieces for the first time there's  even an elden ring art subreddit  specifically dedicated to fan art though  it is a bit smaller than the main one  i hope this video has been a nice  perusing of some of the community's art  and hopefully it has exposed some of you  to the fan art for the first time the  artists deserve a grand congratulations  for their work and if any of these have  really caught your attention you can go  support the artists directly by buying  their work and i apologize to any of the  artists if i mispronounced your name  there's a good chance that that might  have happened  that will do it for this video i just  wanted to make a quick showcase to  spread the word about this great art and  to say another thanks to the artists for  allowing me to use their work on my  channel i hope you've all enjoyed the  video subscribe if you want to see more  and let me know in the comments if you  have a favorite piece of elden ring fan  art this video has been another of the  scheduled pieces i've made because when  this video releases i'm not currently  making videos it's not my core lore or  deep dive but those will continue once i  get back to making videos at the end of  this month thank you all for watching  and i'll see you in the next video peace
 

